    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1930620582250357019",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1930620582250357019",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1930620582250357019",
      "text": "[2:36PM] #Okota_Isolo #TrafficUpdate \n\nThe Cele Ijesha link bridge is clear, and the stretch from Ballet to Ijesha inward Mile 2 is experiencing rapid movement. Similarly, the route from Cele, past the Rain Oil petrol station, to Ago Palace is flowing quickly, with consistent conditions for the return journey.\n\nMotorists can expect fast traffic from 5 Star to the Iyana Isolo underpass, as well as on the Daleko-Mushin bridge. All routes from the LASUTECH roundabout through Limca junction, Aiye, Omonije, College, Ishaga, Mustapha, Ile Ibadan, Ire Akari, and Kogberegbe are experiencing fast-moving traffic in both directions.\n\nAdditionally, the journey from Oke-Afa bridge to Pako is quick, with similar conditions for the return trip. From Pako to Akiti and Chemist bus stops, traffic is moving swiftly, and the return journey is also clear. \n\nLastly, the route from Ago roundabout to Ibeh road is experiencing fast traffic, with smooth conditions for the return. The stretch from Ilasa-Transformer to Apata junction also reports fast traffic in both directions.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
